Z||000000||GTMike||07-02-2001||03:36 AM||||any one live at high elevation and race thier fiero?  i'm just trying to get an idea of what i could run at 5800 feet.  gt 5speed.<P>upgrades i plan on doing are. pullies. low temp fan switch and thermastat.   gasket matching the intake.   free flow exaust.<BR>ebatch lowering springs.   i might even take out the passenger seat  when i race at the strip. <P>i would like to keep up with the mustangs that are running low 15s at this elevation.<P>sorry this is so long.  <BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||07-02-2001||08:32 PM||||I ran the numbers for you on the drag program. At 800-feet a five speed runs a 15.8 @ 86.9 mph and runs 0-60 mph in 8 seconds. At 5800-feet it runs a 16.95 @ 82.2 mph and runs to 0-60 mph in 9.7 seconds. <P>What a difference! At your elevation your car is as fast as a Ford escort is down here. You need to get a turbocharger or move down lower. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTMike||07-03-2001||01:28 AM||||thanks alot. were those numbers for a stock fiero?  or one that has been modified?<P>i'm hoping that i will be able to run mid 15s<BR>up here. thats what the stock mustangs were doing last sunday at the strip.<BR>i now i have alot of mods to do befor that. <P>thanks so much for comeing up with those numbers for me.  ||||reg||1
